    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "West Bengal hosts 6 National Parks: Sundarbans, Buxa, Gorumara, Neora Valley, Singalila, and Jaldapara.",
        "The Sundarbans was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1987 and designated as a Ramsar Site in 2019.",
        "East Calcutta Wetlands (ECW) was recognized as a Ramsar Site in 2002 for its unique natural sewage treatment system.",
        "The State Animal of West Bengal is the Fishing Cat, and the State Tree is Chatim (Alstonia scholaris).",
        "Singalila National Park in Darjeeling district is a critical refuge for the endangered Red Panda."
      ],
      "id": "4txg0bm"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sundarbans was recognized as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1987 and a Ramsar Wetland of International Importance in 2019.",
        "East Calcutta Wetlands (ECW) was designated a Ramsar Site in 2002 and acts as a natural wastewater treatment zone.",
        "Singalila and Neora Valley National Parks are crucial conservation zones for the endangered Red Panda in northern West Bengal."
      ],
